WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
in entrepreneurial activity.

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.400
An entrepreneur examines needs, wants, and problems, and then tries to think about if

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.200
a better solution can be created.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.000
Narrows the possible opportunities down to one specific opportunity.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.600
Thinks of an innovative idea to address the identified opportunity, researches the opportunity

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.600
and idea thoroughly, enlists the best experts, sources of advice and assistance that can be

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.200
found, plans the venture and looks for possible problems that might arise, and weighs

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.800
the risks and possible rewards before making a

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.600
decision.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.300
Never gets tied to a specific idea, even if they personally love it, if research shows

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.100
it's not likely to work.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.100
Employs the resources necessary for the venture if the decision is made to go ahead.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.800
Understands that any entrepreneurial venture will take a great deal of long, hard work.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.100
Realizes a sense of accomplishment from successful ventures and learns lessons for the

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.300
future.

